# Schedule

**File:** `src/yasched/coring/Schedule.py`

Shared base class for all schedule types. Provides a common type for
`Event.schedules` and `Task.schedules` (recurring tasks).

Concrete subclasses each live in their own file:

| Subclass             | File                    | Description                             |
|----------------------|-------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
| `WeeklySchedule`     | `WeeklySchedule.py`     | Repeats on specified days of the week   |
| `MonthlySchedule`    | `MonthlySchedule.py`    | Repeats on a fixed day of the month     |
| `YearlySchedule`     | `YearlySchedule.py`     | Repeats once per year                   |
| `SingleDaySchedule`  | `SingleDaySchedule.py`  | One-off occurrence on a single date     |
| `MultiDaySchedule`   | `MultiDaySchedule.py`   | One-off occurrence spanning multiple days |

---

## Interface

```
Schedule
```

No shared fields or methods. The class exists solely to unify the five concrete
schedule types under one type for use in `list[Schedule]`.

---

## Notes

- Declared as a plain base class without abstract methods.
- All concrete subclasses are frozen dataclasses.
- `Schedule` itself is not a dataclass — subclasses inherit independently.
- `backending` is responsible for computing actual occurrence dates from any
  `Schedule` instance; no date-generation logic lives here.
